.TH LOAMD 1 "2026-11-23" "loam 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
loamd \- per-user supervisor for loam command instances
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loamd
.RI [ serve ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B loamd
.I start \fICOMMAND\fR
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B loamd
.I list\fR|\fIping\fR|\fIinspect\fR|\fIlogs\fR|\fIstop\fR|\fIreload\fR|\fIshutdown
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B loamd
is the per-user supervisor for command and web-surface Spores. It owns a
command registry, a plugin registry, the instances it starts, and the local
static web listener. It accepts only same-uid peers over a Unix socket.
.PP
It also publishes manifest-declared web surfaces as Mycelium service leases
when a Mycelium identity is available. The matching
.B mycelium-frontdoor
derives routes from those leases.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIFILE\fR
Read host defaults from
.IR loam.conf.soil .
.TP
.B \-\-socket \fIPATH\fR
Control socket. Defaults to
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/loam/loamd.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-root \fIDIR\fR
Package root to scan. Repeatable. A first \fB\-\-root\fR replaces roots from the
configuration file; later roots append.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-instances \fIN\fR
Maximum live command instances.
.TP
.B \-\-web\-listen \fIADDR\fR
Static web listener. Defaults to
.IR 127.0.0.1:8799 .
.TP
.B \-\-log\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Directory for durable instance logs.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-max\-bytes \fIN\fR
Rotate an instance log before it grows past \fIN\fR bytes.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-keep \fIN\fR
Keep \fIN\fR rotated generations.
.TP
.B \-\-mycelium\-home \fIDIR\fR
Mycelium state directory used to publish web-surface leases.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-publish\-leases
Serve web surfaces without publishing Mycelium leases.
.TP
.B \-\-image\-runtime \fIPATH\fR
Live Soil image runtime. Defaults to
.I soil-image
on PATH.
.TP
.B \-\-window\-runtime \fIPATH\fR
Native webview host. Defaults to
.I loam-window
on PATH.
.SH CONTROL COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List known instances.
.TP
.B inspect \fIID\fR
Show one instance.
.TP
.B logs \fIID\fR
Return captured stdout/stderr. Falls back to the durable log after restart.
.TP
.B stop \fIID\fR
Stop a running instance.
.TP
.B reload
Rescan command and plugin roots without restarting the daemon. Static web
surfaces are discovered at startup; see the note below.
.TP
.B shutdown
Stop the daemon and its instances.
.SH WEB SURFACES
A web surface is served only when its package declares both a web surface and
an anycast claim. See the Spore manifest documentation or the Soil skill for
the manifest shape. The listener scans roots at startup;
a newly installed web package needs one daemon restart. Static file edits do not.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/loam/loam.conf.soil
Host defaults.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/loam/logs/
Per-instance logs.
.TP
.I ~/.mycelium/application-services.json
Mycelium service observations written by the lease publisher.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
loamd
loamd start hello --name world --id hello-1
loamd logs hello-1
loamd stop hello-1
.fi
.PP
Serve a package root on the local web listener:
.PP
.nf
loamd serve --root ~/.mycelium/spores --web-listen 127.0.0.1:8799
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loam (1),
.BR mycelium-frontdoor (1),
.BR mycelium (1)
